==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[take]] [[away]]|takes away|taking away|took away|taken away}}

# To [[remove]] something and put it in a different place.
#: {{ux|en|Mother '''took''' our plates '''away''' and came back with some fruit for us to eat.}}
# To [[remove]] something, either material or abstract, so that a person no longer has it.
#: {{ux|en|The teacher '''took''' my mobile phone '''away''' until the end of the lesson.}}
#: {{ux|en|The new law will '''take away''' some important rights from immigrant residents.}}
#: {{ux|en|The doctor gave me pills to '''take away''' the pain.}}
# To [[subtract]] or [[diminish]] something.
#: {{ux|en|If I have five apples and you '''take away''' two, how many do I have left?}}
#* {{quote-journal
|date=January 22, 2011
|author=Ian Hughes
|title=Arsenal 3 - 0 Wigan
|work=BBC
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9365488.stm
|page=
|passage=But '''take''' nothing '''away''' from Arsenal, who were driven on by the brilliance of Van Persie and Fabregas and only prevented from being out of sight at half-time by the feats of Al Habsi.}}
# To leave a [[memory]] or [[impression]] in one's mind that you think about later.
#: {{ux|en|I '''took away''' the impression that the play was under rehearsed.}}
# {{label|en|of a person}} To make someone leave a place and go somewhere else. Usually not with the person's [[consent]].
#: {{ux|en|The police '''took''' him '''away''' for questioning.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'm '''taking''' you '''away''' to the country for a rest. It's for your own good!}}
# {{label|en|of a person}} To prevent, or limit, someone from being somewhere, or from doing something.
#: {{ux|en|My job '''takes''' me '''away''' from home most weekends.}}
#: {{ux|en|Using the internet so much can '''take''' you '''away''' from your studies.}}

====Usage notes====
All senses are transitive and the object may appear before or after the particle. If the object is a pronoun, then it must be before the particle.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|To remove something, either material or abstract, so that a person no longer has it.}} [[deprive]], [[divest]], [[dispossess]], [[fortake]], [[strip]]

